  "starterCode": "# MoE Router — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(logits, top_k=1):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **MoE Router** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(logits, top_k=1):\n    x=np.asarray(logits,dtype=float)\n    if top_k<1 or top_k>x.shape[-1]: raise ValueError(\"invalid top_k\")\n    idx=np.argsort(x,axis=-1)[...,-top_k:][...,::-1]\n    vals=np.take_along_axis(x,idx,axis=-1)\n    e=np.exp(vals-vals.max(axis=-1,keepdims=True)); probs=e/e.sum(axis=-1,keepdims=True)\n    return {\"expert_indices\":idx.tolist(),\"weights\":probs.tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
